# Weaver config — copy to `.env` (gitignored) and uncomment what you need.
# Only fills UNSET vars: an explicit `export` in your shell always wins.
# Secrets do NOT belong here — use `weaver secret set <NAME> --ws <slug>` for
# action credentials or `weaver secret set <NAME> --executor` for provider keys.

# --- Models ---------------------------------------------------------------
# The coordinator is the evaluative seat (runs rarely, at the moments that
# matter); workers do the volume. When the coordinator's primary model pool is
# capacity-limited, it degrades down its ordered fallback chain and keeps
# reconciling.
# WEAVER_COORDINATOR_MODEL=claude-fable-5
# WEAVER_COORDINATOR_EXECUTOR=local-sdk
# Ordered fallback seats tried after the primary, as comma-separated
# executor:model entries (models may be provider-qualified with slashes).
# When set, the single-fallback pair below is ignored.
# WEAVER_COORDINATOR_FALLBACKS=local-sdk:claude-opus-5,codex-sdk:gpt-5.6-sol
# Legacy single fallback, used only while WEAVER_COORDINATOR_FALLBACKS is unset:
# WEAVER_COORDINATOR_FALLBACK_MODEL=claude-opus-5
# WEAVER_COORDINATOR_FALLBACK_EXECUTOR=local-sdk
# WEAVER_WORKER_MODEL=sonnet
# Ordered worker capacity ladder tried after the configured WEAVER_EXECUTOR /
# WEAVER_WORKER_MODEL seat when earlier targets are capacity-parked. Same
# entry format; each named executor needs its credentials on this host.
# WEAVER_WORKER_FALLBACKS=codex-sdk:gpt-5.6-sol,pi:zai-coding-plan/glm-5.3,pi:openrouter/moonshotai/kimi-k3
# Performance routes may override the model for typed, eval-proven work inside
# this configured worker substrate. Actions never enter the router.
# WEAVER_ACTION_EXECUTOR=local-sdk
# WEAVER_ACTION_MODEL=sonnet
# WEAVER_ASK_MODEL=sonnet

# --- Storage --------------------------------------------------------------
# Default: fs backend under <repo>/state. Point at Postgres to share one fleet
# across machines, or sqlite for a single-file local store.
# WEAVER_STORE=postgres://user:pass@host:5432/weaver
# WEAVER_HOME=/absolute/path/to/state

# --- Execution / actions --------------------------------------------------
# local-sdk = Claude Code login; codex-sdk = Codex/ChatGPT login;
# pi = pinned host process/API; openhands = container/API.
# WEAVER_EXECUTOR=local-sdk
# A runner claims only its configured seats by default. Declare extra reviewed
# route substrates explicitly on heterogeneous/shared fleets.
# WEAVER_RUNNER_EXECUTORS=local-sdk,codex-sdk,pi,openhands
# API keys live in the executor-only secret file, not .env:
#   weaver secret set OPENROUTER_API_KEY --executor
#   weaver secret set ZHIPU_API_KEY --executor
# WEAVER_OPENHANDS_BASE_URL=https://custom-openai-compatible.example/v1
# WEAVER_PILOT_URL=http://localhost:9721
